{#
	ACF layout: doc_note — Figma `accessibility-contact` (22:196) and the
	heading directly above it, the pair that closes a document page.

	The heading is a field on this layout rather than the last line an editor
	types into the `rich_text` above, and that is the whole reason this is a
	section and not a card floating after the prose. In the frame both live
	inside one `doc-body` band, 40 apart; in Flexible Content each section owns
	its own vertical rhythm, so a heading left in the prose section would end up
	a full band away from the panel it names.

	Named for what it is rather than for the one document that uses it: a
	labelled contact panel at the end of a legal page is the same object on a
	terms or a privacy page.

	The surface is `raised-card` — the revision's resting card, not
	`raised-over-image`: this panel is lifted on a screen with no photo behind
	it, which is exactly the distinction those two mixins carry.
#}

{% if section.label or section.text %}
	<section class="doc-note">
		<div class="container doc-note__inner">

			{% if section.heading %}
				<h2 class="doc-note__heading">{{ section.heading }}</h2>
			{% endif %}

			<div class="doc-note__card">

				{% if section.label %}
					<p class="doc-note__label">{{ section.label }}</p>
				{% endif %}

				{% if section.text %}
					<p class="doc-note__text">{{ section.text }}</p>
				{% endif %}

				{% if section.note %}
					<p class="doc-note__note">{{ section.note }}</p>
				{% endif %}

			</div>

		</div>
	</section>
{% endif %}
